{
  "version": "predicates-v8",
  "description": "Predicates a ProposalDraft may use. Wikidata mappings say which source statements can evidence each predicate: forward means the statement's entity is the assertion subject; inverse means the statement's value is the assertion subject. v2: commanded relates a person to a force (Group), not to an event. v3: authority held over a force (heldAuthorityOver) is separated from command actually exercised (commanded); evidence for one never counts for the other. v4: each predicate declares its qualifiers (context, role, time: none, optional, required, or withRole for time required only when a role is given) and its claim modes; adds the unary occurred and authorOf (22-CLAIM-QUALIFIERS.md). v5: each predicate declares a category (factual or interpretive); kinds Office and Concept; narrative links triggeredBy and resultedIn; interpretive exemplifies and ledTo (attributed only) and depictsSameAs (curator) (23-NARRATIVE-AND-NOTES.md). v6: occurred extends to Period (each source's bounds an attributed claim); subperiodOf and followedBy relate periods; partOf stays Event to Event (24-PERIODS-AND-TRANSFORMATION.md). v7: opposed relates people or groups who were opponents, symmetric, time required, with an optional context event (the war or battle); political, military, or personal opposition is not split. Works carry a form; a claim attributed to a Work of a creative form is imaginative, derived and never chosen (25-LIVES-AND-PLAYGROUND.md section 6). v8: born and died are dated unary claims (no date is a bare property; 25 section 10), from Wikidata P569 and P570; participatedIn also maps P1344 (participant in).",
